MENTOR: That's right. The curve peaks in the middle, which is the shape Easy Ease always gives you.

I tried to grab the frame at 1 s to show you Title mid-move, but the preview didn't come back in a usable form, so I can't describe where Title is on screen. The graph tells the story anyway.

In the speed graph, each keyframe has a handle, and **how far it reaches sideways is the influence: how long the ease lasts.** Easy Ease gives every key the same reach, which is why all four of Title's moves feel the same: slow, fast in the middle, slow.

To give a move more character:
- **A short reach out of the first key** (0.5 s) makes Title get going quickly.
- **A long reach into the landing key** (1.5 s) makes it settle in gently.

Keep the landing handle along the bottom of the graph. If you drag it up, Title arrives still moving.

